{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsW7ZGdcejiYMhoH91AW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019fsUPas5LynunU3Azz4jR4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/p-02/primary/exec-ws/resolution.json","content":"{\n  \"task_id\": \"p-02\",\n  \"topology_id\": \"isolated-child\",\n  \"resolutions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q1\",\n      \"status\": \"RESOLVED\",\n      \"resolved_by\": \"propose-child\",\n      \"answer\": \"None. joinspec.md determines a unique output for every behavior exercised by probes.json: the empty list is fixed verbatim to the empty string (probe 2); a singleton renders as the item itself, since the ', ' separator only occurs between items and the order clause fixes that the item is rendered (probes 0, 4); the separator clause fixes ', ' and the order clause fixes input order for multi-item lists (probes 1, 3, 5). The explicit no-undetermined-behavior argument covering all six probes is recorded in ea-statement.md; undetermined_behaviors is therefore the empty list.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"ev-1\", \"ev-2\"],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-A\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q2\",\n      \"status\": \"RESOLVED\",\n      \"resolved_by\": \"propose-child\",\n      \"answer\": \"Exactly one probe-exercised behavior differs: multi-item ordering. The spec fixes 'the order given' while joiner.py computes ', '.join(reversed(items)). Per-probe: indices 1 (['x','y']: spec 'x, y' vs 'y, x'), 3 (['one','two','three']: spec 'one, two, three' vs 'three, two, one'), and 5 (['b','a']: spec 'b, a' vs 'a, b') differ; indices 0, 2, 4 (singletons and the empty list) coincide because reversal is unobservable there. Separator and empty-list behaviors do not differ. Full table in ea-statement.md.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"ev-1\", \"ev-2\"],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-A\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n      \"status\": \"UNRESOLVED\",\n      \"resolved_by\": \"\",\n      \"answer\": \"Cannot be resolved in this session: E-B requires an implementation authored solely from joinspec.md by an author who has never accessed joiner.py nor any analysis derived from it, and this session has read joiner.py. A child bundle (child/) has been proposed assigning a clean-room implementer whose input manifest contains only package/artifacts/joinspec.md; the deterministic integration rule (child/integration-plan.json) performs the item-level comparison over probes.json after the root-executed launch.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-B\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q4\",\n      \"status\": \"UNRESOLVED\",\n      \"resolved_by\": \"\",\n      \"answer\": \"The verdict is a deterministic function of E-A and E-B jointly (DIVERGES iff the comparison shows a differing output on some probe) and may not be asserted from spec-reading alone; since the admissible E-B comparison does not yet exist, result.json carries verdict = PENDING-INTEGRATION and divergent_probe_indices = PENDING-INTEGRATION. The root-executed verify-integration node settles them by applying the pre-committed rule in child/integration-plan.json.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-C\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2449,"cache_read_input_tokens":53176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2449},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db66dc51-f7c6-488d-b329-2a1d62a73761","uuid":"81829dfa-c4d1-42bd-928e-317a285eeece","timestamp":"2026-08-09T16:38:15.773Z","request_id":"req_011CdsW7ScXmVjXsNKo71MjK"}
